# Visual design and copy

The site must look designed, not generated. **The site is eight slates.**
Details live in `BLUEPRINT.md` §8–§10 and §15. Do not invent a ninth palette.

## Color and type

- Default system: **Slates Dark** tokens from the blueprint (§8.2)
- Page ground: `#000000` or `#131313`. Not dark gray-blue
- Links inherit the **current section accent**, not a global blue
- Home and `/support` stay dark and colorful. `/privacy` may use Slates Light
  washes for long reading — not a light-mode corporate marketing page
- Self-hosted or system fonts only. Light headlines (200–400), not heavy black
  type on neon

## Layout and motion

- Full-bleed color bands; copy stays in ~40–44rem measure
- Numbered 1–8 circles are as important as color; do not convey meaning by
  color alone
- Real product photography, not stock, AI device frames, or 3D blobs. The
  owner’s licensed device mockups in `resources/mockups/` are allowed when
  they show a real Slates capture (`BLUEPRINT.md` §8.5)
- Motion answers the visitor and never plays on its own: no autoplay, no
  looping video, no timed carousels (`BLUEPRINT.md` §8.7)
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` disables motion. No scroll-jacking

If a section could live on a generic startup template (Inter + Lucide +
“supercharged”), it is not done.

## Copy

Calm, specific, a little proud. Author: **Miguel Dovale**. English only for v1.
Home subtitle: *Eight color-coded scratchpads for quick capture.* Feature
grid maps one feature to each slot color (`BLUEPRINT.md` §9.1). Footer on
every page: Support · Privacy · Email · © Miguel Dovale.

## Accessibility

Contrast for body and footer gray; focus rings on App Store and mailto;
real `alt` text; VoiceOver-linear `/support` and `/privacy`.
